## Spec B1, B7 (docs/specs/stdlib/executor.spec.md): block_on
## drives a sub-phase-2A future (no `.await`) to completion. The
## async_lowering rewriter erases `block_on(make_int())` at AST
## time and replaces with an inline poll-yield loop. The future is
## a single-state machine returning Poll.Ready(42) on its first
## poll, so block_on returns immediately without ever spinning.
##
## Pinned behaviours:
##   B1 — `block_on(future)` is a callable free function.
##   B2 — Inlined poll loop calls `(&var fut).poll(&var ctx)` and
##        matches Poll.Ready(v) → exit / Poll.Pending → yield.
##   B7 — End-to-end: block_on returns the future's Ready payload.

async def make_int() -> Int
  42
end

def main
  let result = block_on(make_int())
  puts "#{result}"
end
